  "version": 1,
  "title": "Integration in algebraically closed valued fields",
  "abstract": "Two geometric preparation theorems for integration in algebraically closed valued fields. Proposition 3.19 partitions an original-base definable VF bijection into finitely many definable pieces on which it is open-to-open. Lemma 4.8 decomposes an original-Gamma-base definable subset of VF squared into two-cell fibres of a definable map to a finite RV power. The cell positioning graph and both paradigms are definable over the original base together with the output RV tuple. Actual saturation, characteristic, parameter-base and named-value hypotheses remain in the formal statements. The larger repository develops Sections 2–7, including ordinary and measured integration; those additional results are outside this Palomar selection.",
